[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879381491","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3879381491","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3879381491,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nOqnz","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T16:59:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T16:59:27Z","body":"Okay, this does not seem to be specific to Arrays, also happens with e.g. Vector2. It seems that the connect method checks for equality with the default equality comparator, so any two objects for which (a = b) is true, this method will assume they are the same object, even if they are not.\n\ngonna extend the example script\n(I know there isn't really any method on a Vector2 that you woul ever want to connect to a signal, but just to show it's not specific to Arrays)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879381491/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879392807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3879392807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3879392807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nOtYn","user":{"login":"mikest","id":742517,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/742517?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest","html_url":"https://github.com/mikest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T17:00:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:00:49Z","body":"Yeah, this is function is using the default comparitor, should check if the signal dispatch is also using the same comparitor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879392807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879574319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3879574319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3879574319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nPZsv","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T17:21:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:26:57Z","body":"This is also true for Dictionaries, and at first I thought there was an issue with Dictionaries and Callables, because trying to connect to the signal with `something.connect(dict.erase)` leads to the following runtime error: `Invalid access to property or key 'erase' on a base object of type 'Dictionary'.` Which of course happens because it's looking for a key with the value \"erase\" in the dictionary instead.\nThe documentation has the correct way to deal with that: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/classes/class_callable.html\nwhich is `Callable.create(dictionary, \"clear\")`.\n\nThis is not related to this issue, but I just wanted to mention it here, because I'm too tired to create another issue lobbying for this, but I would appreciate if the error message would mention how to deal with Callables on Dictionaries or pointed one in the right direction of the docs.\n\n(Also worth pointing out: the Callable docs make mention of the Dictionary exception, but the Dictionary docs make no mention of being an exception to how Callable works with them)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879574319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879592589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3879592589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3879592589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nPeKN","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T17:23:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:23:29Z","body":"> Yeah, this is function is using the default comparitor, should check if the signal dispatch is also using the same comparitor.\n\nI don't see why signal dispatch would need a comparator? It probably just has a list of all connected callables, and calls them one after the other. This check really is only there on the 'connect' call is what I would assume.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3879592589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3880014934","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3880014934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3880014934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nRFRW","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T18:39:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T18:40:00Z","body":"> It seems that the connect method checks for equality with the default equality comparator\n\nIt's worse, the comparison is hash based. So you can get an error for arrays with different contents (at the time of connecting), or even for completely different Variant+method pairs:\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends EditorScript\n\nsignal sig\n\nfunc _run() -> void:\n\ttest1()\n\ttest2()\n\nfunc test1() -> void:\n\tvar a1 := [9, 2, 4, 7, 0, 3, 8, 6, 1, 5]\n\tvar a2 := [3, 1, 0, 2, 6, 9, 7, 5, 8, 4]\n\tprint(hash(a1.front)) # 3502896893\n\tprint(hash(a2.front)) # 3502896893\n\n\tsig.connect(a1.front)\n\tsig.connect(a2.front) # ERROR: Signal 'sig' is already connected to given callable 'Array::front' in that object.\n\nfunc test2() -> void:\n\tvar a := [6, 8, 4, 3, 7, 0, 9, 5, 1, 2]\n\tvar v := Vector2i(66193, 0)\n\tprint(hash(a.front)) # 725976081\n\tprint(hash(v.abs)) # 725976081\n\t\n\tsig.connect(a.front)\n\tsig.connect(v.abs) # ERROR: Signal 'sig' is already connected to given callable 'Vector2i::abs' in that object.\n```\n\n\n> This issue was already raised in: [#97044](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/97044) but dismissed there with \"you can't connect the same method of the same object to the same signal\" which is not relevant here as these are clearly two different arrays, as testcase 0 and 5 in the script below thoroughly highlight.\n\n@AThousandShips AFAICT #97044 was closed incorrectly, the justification there doesn't match the MRP (\"connecting the same method of 2 different arrays\" is not the same as \"connecting the same method of the same object twice\"). Not sure how this should be handled triage-wise.\n\n---\n\nThis seems to fix the issue:\n\n```diff\n--- a/core/variant/variant_callable.cpp\n+++ b/core/variant/variant_callable.cpp\n@@ -33,7 +33,12 @@\n #include \"core/templates/hashfuncs.h\"\n\n bool VariantCallable::compare_equal(const CallableCustom *p_a, const CallableCustom *p_b) {\n-       return p_a->hash() == p_b->hash();\n+       if (p_a->hash() != p_b->hash()) {\n+               return false;\n+       }\n+       const VariantCallable *vca = static_cast<const VariantCallable *>(p_a);\n+       const VariantCallable *vcb = static_cast<const VariantCallable *>(p_b);\n+       return vca->variant.identity_compare(vcb->variant) && vca->method == vcb->method;\n }\n```\n\nI'm not sure about the implications / whether it's fully sufficient etc. though, so leaving it up for the core folks.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3880014934/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3880061651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3880061651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3880061651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nRQrT","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T18:49:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T18:49:48Z","body":"> AFAICT https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/97044 was closed incorrectly, the justification there doesn't match the MRP (\"connecting the same method of 2 different arrays\" is not the same as \"connecting the same method of the same object twice\"). Not sure how this should be handled triage-wise.\n\nBased it on the feedback of another contributor who had tested it, the issue didn't contain enough information on its own","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3880061651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894019202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3894019202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3894019202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oGgSC","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T23:50:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T00:11:01Z","body":"@kleonc I know this is offtopic but I just gotta ask: how did you find hash collissions for your example so quickly?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894019202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894078898","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-3894078898","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":3894078898,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oGu2y","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T00:10:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T00:11:08Z","body":"> [@kleonc](https://github.com/kleonc) I know this is offtopic but I just gotta ask: how did you find hash collissions for your example so quickly?\n\n@klianc09 Nothing fancy, pretty much brute force:\n```gdscript\nfunc foo() -> void:\n\tvar d := {}\n\tfor i in 100_000:\n\t\tvar a := range(10)\n\t\ta.shuffle()\n\t\tvar h := hash(a.front)\n\t\tvar prev_a = d.get(h)\n\t\tif prev_a != null and a != prev_a:\n\t\t\tprint(a)\n\t\t\tprint(d[h])\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\td[h] = a\n\tfor i in 0x7fff_ffff_ffff_ffff:\n\t\tvar h := hash(Vector2i(i, 0).abs)\n\t\tif h in d:\n\t\t\tprint(Vector2i(i, 0))\n\t\t\tprint(d[h])\n\t\t\tbreak\n\tprint(\"finished\")\n```\n(I'm marking both comments as off-topic)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894078898/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4041890214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116141#issuecomment-4041890214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116141","id":4041890214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7w6lmm","user":{"login":"Arthurmtro","id":55857849,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODU3ODQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55857849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro","html_url":"https://github.com/Arthurmtro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arthurmtro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T20:08:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T20:08:30Z","body":"Opened #117336 with a fix for this, based on the approach @kleonc suggested. Added a unit test as well.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4041890214/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]